---
description: "PixelForge non-negotiable global constraints"
alwaysApply: true
---
# Security red lines (violation = bug)
- Never expose CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT, OBJECT_STORAGE_SECRET_KEY, or any server secret in frontend code
- Never use subprocess(shell=True) with user input
- Never trust file extensions alone. Validate MIME + magic bytes
- All FFmpeg calls must use argument arrays (spawn/execa). No string concatenation
- Cross-user data access is a security defect. Every Convex query must filter by userId

# Architecture boundaries
- The Python service never writes directly to Convex. State updates flow through the Node API
- ProcessingProvider is the ONLY legal processing entry point. Routes must not call Python directly
- Object storage secret key lives only in Node API env vars. Python reads/writes via signed URLs

# Forbidden
- No committed .env files
- No fake progress bars or fake processing states
- No heavy dependencies not declared in the architecture doc
